Executive Summary
During the final integration phase of the "GameZone Unicesar" system, AI was utilized as an interactive pair-programming assistant. The primary goal was to connect the core architectural layers (Model, Persistence, Service, and UI) using Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) principles in Java. The AI helped clarify fundamental Java concepts, resolve method signature mismatches across modules, and generate clean UI components.

Key Learning Objectives & Concept Reminders
Dependency Injection & Layered Architecture: Reinforcing how repositories feed into service layers, which are then passed into the UI driver (ConsoleMenu) via the entry point (Main).

Constructor Overloading & Argument Signatures: Resolving compiler issues where model classes (Sale, Customer, Seller) required exact parameter types and counts.

Java Generics & Collections: Fixing list type declarations (List) to ensure strong typing across services and UI views.

Package Structure Standards: Ensuring the Main.java class resides in the root package (com.gamezone) rather than nested sub-packages to properly orchestrate all application modules.

